  - m_Id: 351479409856549
    m_Localized: Trading & Auction Guide
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 351479409856550
    m_Localized: Beetle store / Collection market / Public auctions
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 351479409856551
    m_Localized: "1. Store and mailbox\nLive beetles, framed specimens and supplies
      have fixed prices. Buy supplies in batches of 1\u201399. Claim orders by mail:
      beetles enter storage, specimens enter your collection.\n\n2. Instant sales\nStore
      buyback: 55% of adult market value (larvae 35%), 60% for specimens, and 40%
      of supply retail price. The displayed amount is your final payout.\n\n3. Trading
      BBS\nHealthy adults and specimens share listing slots. Listing is free; offers
      refresh weekly. Completed sales incur a 5% fee. Withdraw any time before selling.
      Listed specimens leave the display wall.\n\n4. Public auctions\nEach lot lasts
      four rounds. Enter a bid, then advance the round for rival responses. Only
      the highest bidder at closing can win. Bids at or above expectation always
      succeed; below it, acceptance equals the bid/expectation ratio squared. Bids
      are held in escrow and refunded if outbid or rejected.\n\n5. Weekly stock and
      saves\nNext week settles unfinished auctions and refreshes stock. Every successful
      trade is saved. Alt+T: theme menu; Alt+M: light/dark; Alt+H: help."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
